            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0120" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 56.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 248.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 5, 1870</date>. (Received August 17,
                    1870.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    printed copy of a dispatch addressed by his excellency the Duke de Gramont,
                    minister of foreign affairs, to the diplomatic agents of France at foreign
                    courts, on the subject of the treaty said to have been proposed by the Emperor
                    of the French to the government of the North German Confederacy. It is taken
                    from the columns of Galignani of this day.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d56-a1.xml" xpointer="d56-a1"/>
